WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.760
Look directly down from above, just as we finish reversing parallel to the curb.

00:05.380 --> 00:11.440
As the car reverses around center X, the wheels at E and F travel along the two dashed circles.

00:12.020 --> 00:16.180
Meanwhile, the front left corner A of our car sweeps along the outer circle.

00:16.600 --> 00:21.920
In the tightest possible parking space, that corner A will just barely miss the corner G

00:21.920 --> 00:23.300
of the car parked in front.

00:23.920 --> 00:27.860
Because corner A passes right through point G along that outer circle,

00:27.860 --> 00:32.340
both A and G lie at the exact same distance from the center X.

